// "+1/+1 for each <selection>" scaled pump ([CR#613.4c] layer 7c, [CR#107.3]
// "for each"). Predicate slot = the selection noun ("Forest you control");
// Objects+CountOf wrap it ONCE and forward into `PowerAndToughnessBoth` (its
// single `NumericOp` param), so BOTH axes share the same computed count
// without repeating the `CountOf(Objects(...))` construction — genuinely two
// real scaling axes, unlike the `P·0` family below. Render flattens this
// through the structural `for_each_pump_clause` arm — the template is
// parse-only.
(
    name: "P1P1ForEach",
    template: "gets +1/+1 for each ${0}",
    kinds: [Modification],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: PowerAndToughnessBoth(Up(CountOf(Objects(Param(0))))),
)
